<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:57:15 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident</link><description>
A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0872f008-c1be-11f1-902a-15b8d05e51cb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:51:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Calls to block social media platforms for minors in France amid school protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/calls-to-block-social-media-platforms-for-minors-in-france-amid-school-protests</link><description>
One factor accelerating these student protest is social media, and its being boosted even more by artificial intelligence. Some French mayors have even called for social media platforms to be temporarily blocked for minors. Our colleauges at France 2 took a look at the impact
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cdb0260-c1bc-11f1-99d1-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-201158-201334-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cdb0260-c1bc-11f1-99d1-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-201158-201334-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41e16dee-c1bc-11f1-9d5e-09f3696b54d5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:47:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason</link><description>
A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a786f758-c1bd-11f1-b53b-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-204356-204757-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a786f758-c1bd-11f1-b53b-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-204356-204757-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ada39420-c1bd-11f1-9396-37dc3b8a76ed</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:42:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'We're fed up': Paris students rise up in a movement that shows no sign of slowing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261006-we-re-fed-up-paris-students-rise-up-in-a-movement-that-shows-no-sign-of-slowing</link><description>
Hundreds of thousands of students and their supporters took part in nationwide protests across France on Tuesday after weeks of student barricades protesting school conditions. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63556510-c1b3-11f1-afe5-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/PXL-20261006-081951850.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63556510-c1b3-11f1-afe5-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/PXL-20261006-081951850.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed7d82ac-c1a1-11f1-ae39-b98d27143737</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:41:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63556510-c1b3-11f1-afe5-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/PXL-20261006-081951850.jpg">© Paul Millar, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Students, unions and teachers in mass movement to demand better learning conditions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/students-unions-and-teachers-in-mass-movement-to-demand-better-learning-conditions</link><description>
A quarter of a million demonstrators took to the streets across France on Tuesday as unions and teachers joined high school students demanding better learning conditions in protests that later descended into sporadic clashes with security forces. A French policeman was on Tuesday charged with violence over the firing of a tear gas grenade last week at close range at a 14-year-old student during the high school protests that have shaken the country, the prosecutor said. Reporting from central Paris, FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin says the protesters are adamant that "this is not it, this movement will continue, we want concrete actions from the government".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0beb092a-c1bc-11f1-8bae-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-200210-200937-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0beb092a-c1bc-11f1-8bae-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-200210-200937-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11801f06-c1bc-11f1-878d-294745f0dd6c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:39:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>France erupts overs schools: Why the violence surrounding surprise movement?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261006-france-erupts-overs-schools-why-the-violence-surrounding-surprise-movement</link><description>
It’s a protest movement that a broke, lame-duck French government did not see coming. Civil servants this Tuesday joining high schoolers now in their third week of picketing over long-deteriorating classroom conditions. The usual recipe for wearing down movements in France has recently been to match eventual violence with a heavy hand, the escalation turning the silent majority against the protesters as was the case with the pre-Covid Yellow Vests movement. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17fac87a-c1af-11f1-8ffe-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-06T130103Z-1056047386-RC2KXNAWGAT3-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17fac87a-c1af-11f1-8ffe-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-06T130103Z-1056047386-RC2KXNAWGAT3-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f005e136-c1b0-11f1-ae87-bb10233b79de</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:12:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Colossal failure: Death penalty system in America is a broken process from start to finish'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/colossal-failure-death-penalty-system-in-america-is-a-broken-process-from-start-to-finish</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Reed Brody, international human rights lawyer and former New York assistant attorney general. According to Brody, the botched execution of Christa Pike reflects a much larger problem: the relationship between capital punishment, institutional failure, due process, and human dignity. The technical failure of lethal injection exposes weaknesses throughout the legal architecture surrounding the death penalty, from the quality and adequacy of defense representation to the profound disparities between jurisdictions and the difficulties states face in administering executions. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7328256-c1a9-11f1-bbbf-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261002-210915-211550-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7328256-c1a9-11f1-bbbf-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261002-210915-211550-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc45820c-c1a9-11f1-b04e-2f0c78429203</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 17:50:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261006-brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says</link><description>
Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d892e40-c1a6-11f1-b146-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-223111-224225-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d892e40-c1a6-11f1-b146-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-223111-224225-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28cc76a0-c1a8-11f1-8dc1-178bc905adef</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 17:05:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil 'has moved to the right progressively over the last two decades', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-has-moved-to-the-right-progressively-over-the-last-two-decades-expert-says</link><description>
Senator Flavio Bolsonaro received on Monday endorsements ​from Ronaldo Caiado and Romeu Zema, two right-wing politicians who ran against him in Sunday's first-round vote, ​for ‌the runoff against President Luiz ⁠Inacio Lula da Silva later this month. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Anthony Pereira, Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies at Tulane University, says that "Lula's path to victory lies in mobilising voters who didn't vote in the first round" while Flavio Bolsonaro "will probably benefit from the voters who voted for other right-wing candidates and who will simply migrate to him, so it looks a lot easier for Flavio to win the second round than it does for Lula".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d892e40-c1a6-11f1-b146-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-223111-224225-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d892e40-c1a6-11f1-b146-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-223111-224225-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a24ccc34-c1a6-11f1-a3b2-d7b89b0ca66e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 17:03:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Paramount completes takeover of Warner Bros, creating media behemoth Skydance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261006-paramount-completes-takeover-of-warner-bros-creating-media-behemoth-skydance</link><description>
Paramount completed its acquisition of Warner Bros Discover on Tuesday, after a bidding war against Netflix. The deal closed following federal approval of a settlement between Paramount and 12 US states that tried to block the transaction on antitrust grounds. Opponents in the movie industry warned of job cuts, while media groups said Warner-owned CNN's independence could be compromised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a237a52-c1a0-11f1-963b-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264700134408.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a237a52-c1a0-11f1-963b-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264700134408.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9cd7d7ca-c19d-11f1-9d87-1fcab5c90ae7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 16:23:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a237a52-c1a0-11f1-963b-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264700134408.jpg">© Chris Pizzello, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tens of thousands demand better education in demonstrations across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tens-of-thousands-demand-better-education-in-demonstrations-across-france</link><description>
Tens of thousands of demonstrators took to the streets across France on Tuesday, as unions and teachers joined high school students who for days have been demanding better learning conditions in protests punctuated by violent confrontations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/effbb778-c19d-11f1-a997-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-163208-163348-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/effbb778-c19d-11f1-a997-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-163208-163348-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f55bdee6-c19d-11f1-9f67-879f772562b6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 16:04:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Norway eyes temporary ban of smart glasses</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-norway-eyes-temporary-ban-of-smart-glasses</link><description>
Norway's government said Monday it wants a temporary ban on the use of smart glasses in certain public places, citing privacy concerns, notably recording images without the knowledge of those filmed. The ban could apply to parks, beaches, museums, shopping centres, schools, daycare centres, healthcare facilities, gyms and public events.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36bbe676-c19c-11f1-b122-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-153429-153610-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36bbe676-c19c-11f1-b122-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-153429-153610-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c47a2a6-c19c-11f1-858f-013d5bfb7ac6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 16:03:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Tense' atmosphere as tens of thousands join French student protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-tense-atmosphere-as-tens-of-thousands-join-french-student-protests</link><description>
Police fired tear gas at ​protesters blockading French high schools on Tuesday as students, teachers and parents took to the streets on the biggest day of action in a wave of demonstrations against understaffed and dilapidated classrooms. Reporting from a march in Paris, France 24's Claire Paccalin says that the demonstration there has been peaceful so far, though the atmosphere is "tense" with a "heavy police presence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f9996be-c19d-11f1-a944-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-160224-160607-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f9996be-c19d-11f1-a944-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-160224-160607-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1426fd70-c19d-11f1-8830-8f94d9f6995e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 16:02:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine fires nearly 900 drones at Russia, says Moscow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-ukraine-fires-nearly-900-drones-at-russia-says-moscow</link><description>
Russian air defenses intercepted nearly 900 Ukrainian drones overnight over multiple regions of the country, as well as the occupied Crimean Peninsula and the Sea of Azov, the Defense Ministry in Moscow said Tuesday. If the figures accurate, it would make it one of the largest Ukrainian drone strikes on Russia since the start of the war, says France 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/333470fa-c19b-11f1-9d6f-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-152736-153355-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/333470fa-c19b-11f1-9d6f-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-152736-153355-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38495524-c19b-11f1-9647-df0f08926322</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 16:01:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Paris Fashion Week: Nicole Kidman, Dua Lipa and Rihanna light up the front row</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261006-paris-fashion-week-nicole-kidman-dua-lipa-and-rihanna-light-up-the-front-row</link><description>
Paris is once again the centre of planet fashion, as the spring-summer 2027 collections take over the catwalks. Simon Moritz takes us through the big hitters, starting with Matthieu Blazy’s exploration of the different women who made up Gabrielle Chanel, as he goes from strength to strength at the prestigious fashion house. We also discuss the comings and goings at YSL, Balenciaga and Dior, and meet Lithuanian designer Juozas Statkevicius as he puts his national heritage in the spotlight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01a2b490-c18a-11f1-88ea-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-06-10-2026-11-59-ING18-CLEAN-N3-frame-25111.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01a2b490-c18a-11f1-88ea-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/ENG-NEWS-06-10-2026-11-59-ING18-CLEAN-N3-frame-25111.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5607d76-c188-11f1-8b46-ad89d048fe22</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:56:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marion CHAVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Kenya reports first-ever Ebola death after patient returns from DR Congo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261006-kenya-reports-first-ever-ebola-death-after-patient-returns-from-dr-congo</link><description>
Kenya on Tuesday reported its first-ever Ebola death after a Kenyan national who had been living in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DR Congo) died after returning to the country. Kenya is the fourth country to record an Ebola case in the current outbreak, which was declared in eastern DR Congo in mid-May.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f9c5870-c196-11f1-8894-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279506107815.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f9c5870-c196-11f1-8894-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279506107815.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29cacdc4-c197-11f1-9d53-79f422015548</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:41:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f9c5870-c196-11f1-8894-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279506107815.jpg">© Andrew Kasuku, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1f7defb8-be59-11f1-b751-855272092b6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:01:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French students looking for protests 'to become a major movement'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261006-french-students-looking-for-protests-to-become-a-major-movement</link><description>
Tens of thousands of demonstrators marched in cities across France on Tuesday in support of protests by school pupils demanding more education funding, increasing pressure on the government of outgoing President Emmanuel Macron. With teachers and trade unions joining the march, the students are seeking to turn the protests into a "major social movement" to increase pressure on the government, says France 24's Marc Perelman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/443e6cdc-c193-11f1-b446-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-150435-151018-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/443e6cdc-c193-11f1-b446-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-150435-151018-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">496e7bca-c193-11f1-91a2-23727062d0ff</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 14:49:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: French PM denies 'police repression', suspends classes as clashes erupt at student protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-live-tens-of-thousands-expected-at-paris-protests-as-unions-join-students</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">3cadd7e8-c191-11f1-81b1-49e5993a4390</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 14:21:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Busification': Inside Ukraine’s controversial recruitment practices</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-busification-inside-ukraine-s-controversial-recruitment-practices</link><description>
Recent reports and videos of alleged recruitment irregularities are fuelling tensions between mobilisation authorities and Ukrainian society, while raising questions about the oversight and implementation of military recruitment.
